{title: 247 - Come, My Way}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F7/C]There is a name I love [Bb]to hear,
[Cm]I love to [F7]sing its worth;
[F7]It sounds like music [Bb]in my ear,
[Bb]The sweetest name on earth.

Refrain:
[F/A]O, how I [Gm]love Jesus,
[Bb]O, how I [Eb]love Jesus,
[Eb]O, how [Ab]I love [Eb]Jesus-
[F]Because He first loved me!

Verse 2:
[F7/C]It tells me of a Savior's [Bb]love,
[Cm]Who died to [F7]set me free;
[F7]It tells me of [Bb]His precious blood,
[Bb]The sinner's perfect plea.

Verse 3:
[F7/C]It tells of One whose loving [Bb]heart
[Cm]Can feel my [F7]deepest woe,
[F7]Who in each sorrow [Bb]bears a part
[Bb]That none can bear below.
